<BaseLayout
  title="About | Qixuan Ding"
  description="A blurb about who I am, and what I want to do."
>
  <h1>About</h1>

  <div class="about-content">
    <section aria-labelledby="about-me">
      <div class="prose">
        <p>Hi, I'm Qixuan.</p>

        <p>
          I'm originally from Calgary, and now I'm a freshman at the University
          of Waterloo studying software engineering.
        </p>

        <p>
          Previously, I've been involved in math and physics competitions,
          scientific research, machine learning, leadership, and policy.
        </p>

        <p>
          My interest in quantitative problem-solving has led me to earn
          national-level awards in competitions, in addition to three Canadian
          Mathematical Olympiad qualifications, an Asian Pacific Mathematical
          Olympiad qualification, and invitations to both Canada’s IMO training
          camp and Canada's national physics camp.
        </p>

        <p>
          It also inspired me to work with professors and PhD researchers in a
          bioinformatics research group at the University of Calgary. I
          programmed and simulated models, analyzed experimental results,
          created data visualizations, and contributed to manuscript preparation
          on machine learning applications in genomic prediction and
          genotype-phenotype association studies, which resulted in two
          co-authored papers published in the Journal of Applied Statistics and
          IEEE Transactions on Computational Biology and Bioinformatics.
        </p>

        <p>
          I'm currently involved as a Core Team Member at UWaterloo's AI design
          team (Wat.ai), investigating ML models and metrics for offball attacks
          in soccer (attacking players without possession), and programming the
          workflow to implement simulations and training.
        </p>

        <p>
          Additionally, I'm documenting my journey through writing and
          potentially on social media in the future. I hope some of my writing
          resonates with you, especially if you are also a student.
        </p>

        <p>
          Moving forward, I'm interested in working on frontier AI, machine
          learning, startups, quant development, and trading strategies. My
          experiences have taught me quantitative problem-solving, teamwork, and
          big-picture thinking, and I hope to apply them in whichever domain I
          choose to work in.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

